{"id": "benefit-errors-dwarf-fraud-found", "title": "Food aid tripled; an eighth was paid in error in 2025; almost no one is disqualified", "seconds": 137.1, "voice": "elevenlabs:OUMCzFUTd0F4Q6lkLkco", "narrator": "Roxy", "tempo": 1.2, "made": "2026-11-24", "key": "7245ffcc62b6a9c5", "words": 425, "beats": [{"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[0]"], "text": "CalFresh is food aid. Most people call it food stamps. In San Francisco, it has tripled.", "t0": 0.2, "t1": 5.0, "shot": "b0", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "money", "label": "CalFresh", "sub": "food aid, often called food stamps"}, "emph": ["tripled"], "wt": [0.0, 0.54, 0.67, 0.93, 1.57, 1.8, 2.04, 2.22, 2.32, 2.57, 3.16, 3.34, 3.56, 4.07, 4.18, 4.33]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["story[1]", "amount"], "text": "So we asked: how much of it is paid in the wrong amount each year?", "t0": 5.12, "t1": 8.99, "shot": "b1", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "Paid in the wrong amount", "sub": "fiscal 2026"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.21, 0.35, 1.27, 1.46, 1.67, 1.74, 1.84, 1.96, 2.24, 2.32, 2.39, 2.62, 2.92, 3.15]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["amount", "suspicious[0].what"], "text": "About 30 million dollars, at the 2025 rate.", "t0": 8.99, "t1": 11.93, "shot": "b2", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$29,675,774", "label": "estimated paid in error, fiscal 2026", "sub": "12% of $247,298,114: the rate of the federal year to September 2025"}, "emph": ["About"], "wt": [0.04, 0.34, 0.63, 0.95, 1.4, 1.55, 1.63, 1.98, 2.57]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "caveat", "ref": ["caveat"], "text": "This is a lead, not a finding.", "t0": 12.45, "t1": 13.89, "shot": "b3", "visual": {"type": "caveat", "line": "This is a lead, not a finding: a pattern in public records. This film says what the records show, what they do not show, and what would settle it."}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.3, 0.38, 0.7, 0.86, 0.93]}, {"scene": "open", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["oneLine"], "text": "And how much fraud did investigators find? 466,321 dollars.", "t0": 14.01, "t1": 19.65, "shot": "b4", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["paid in error, at 12%", "about $30 million"], "b": ["fraud found", "$466,321"]}, "emph": ["466,321"], "wt": [0.0, 0.18, 0.32, 0.54, 0.86, 1.02, 1.66, 2.41, 2.69, 3.01, 3.62, 4.07, 4.3, 4.56, 5.04]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "count", "ref": ["story[0]", "established[0]", "established[1]"], "text": "Food aid grew from 30,021 households to 80,256.", "t0": 19.87, "t1": 24.71, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "80,256", "label": "households on food aid, fiscal 2026 (30,021 in 2019)"}, "emph": ["80,256"], "wt": [0.0, 0.36, 0.64, 0.88, 1.09, 1.37, 1.74, 2.22, 2.74, 2.89, 3.17, 3.55, 3.75, 4.06]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "count", "ref": ["story[0]"], "text": "The money grew from 79.2 million dollars to 247.3 million.", "t0": 24.83, "t1": 29.41, "shot": "b6", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "80,256", "label": "households on food aid, fiscal 2026 (30,021 in 2019)"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.34, 0.54, 0.73, 1.3, 1.54, 1.74, 2.04, 2.4, 2.5, 2.69, 3.04, 3.62, 3.87, 4.11]}, {"scene": "found", "kind": "count", "ref": ["established[2]"], "text": "Computer matches sent to investigators rose only from 251 to 322.", "t0": 29.53, "t1": 34.39, "shot": "b7", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "322", "label": "computer-match referrals to investigators, fiscal 2026 (251 in 2018)"}, "emph": ["322"], "wt": [0.0, 0.44, 0.8, 1.02, 1.11, 1.75, 2.0, 2.22, 2.4, 2.59, 2.91, 3.57, 3.74, 3.96, 4.2]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "share", "ref": ["suspicious[0]"], "text": "The first lead: in the year to September 2025, 12 percent of dollars were paid wrong.", "t0": 34.61, "t1": 39.49, "shot": "b8", "visual": {"type": "share", "pct": 12, "label": "of food-aid dollars paid in the wrong amount, federal year to September 2025"}, "emph": ["12 percent"], "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.4, 1.09, 1.26, 1.34, 1.54, 1.63, 2.08, 2.37, 2.99, 3.35, 3.69, 3.77, 4.14, 4.28, 4.5]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["story[1]"], "text": "That counts money paid too high and too low. Most of it is mistakes, not deceit.", "t0": 39.61, "t1": 43.89, "shot": "b9", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "most of it is mistakes by the agency or the applicant"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.46, 0.72, 0.95, 1.15, 1.44, 1.57, 1.75, 2.43, 2.71, 2.79, 2.88, 2.99, 3.62, 3.83]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "chain", "ref": ["story[0]", "established[3]"], "text": "So why does it matter? The benefits are federal money. But the county decides who qualifies, and for how much.", "t0": 44.01, "t1": 50.47, "shot": "b10", "visual": {"type": "chain", "steps": [{"art": "money", "name": "Federal food-aid program", "sub": "pays the benefits"}, {"art": "cityhall", "name": "Human Services Agency", "sub": "decides who gets how much"}, {"art": "gavel", "name": "From 2028", "sub": "a high error rate costs the State"}], "kicker": "Who pays for mistakes"}, "emph": ["county decides"], "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.33, 0.5, 0.6, 1.4, 1.57, 2.07, 2.26, 2.62, 3.46, 3.65, 3.74, 4.07, 4.54, 4.73, 5.49, 5.68, 5.85, 6.04]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[3]", "story[1]"], "text": "The Food Research & Action Center reports a 2025 law:", "t0": 50.59, "t1": 54.07, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "The federal penalty line: 6%", "kicker": "The first lead"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.36, 0.77, 0.89, 1.26, 1.54, 1.9, 1.95, 2.25, 2.81]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["established[3]", "story[1]"], "text": "a state at 6 percent or more must pay part of the benefits itself, starting in 2028.", "t0": 54.07, "t1": 58.49, "shot": "b11", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "The federal penalty line: 6%", "kicker": "The first lead"}, "emph": ["6 percent"], "wt": [0.04, 0.16, 0.42, 0.52, 0.77, 1.1, 1.23, 1.46, 1.66, 1.85, 2.07, 2.15, 2.23, 2.64, 3.1, 3.45, 3.53, 3.83]}, {"scene": "lead1", "kind": "versus", "ref": ["suspicious[0].why", "suspicious[0].what", "established[5]", "innocent[4]", "notEstablished[4]"], "text": "In 2025, it was twice that line. Since October, it’s running at 5 percent.", "t0": 58.61, "t1": 62.83, "shot": "b12", "visual": {"type": "versus", "a": ["Federal year to September 2025", "12%"], "b": ["Running, October 2025 to April 2026", "5%"], "kicker": "The first lead · the penalty line is 6%"}, "emph": ["twice"], "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.4, 0.95, 1.01, 1.13, 1.48, 1.69, 2.22, 2.51, 2.93, 3.09, 3.36, 3.48, 3.75]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]"], "text": "The second lead: fraud found fell, then rose.", "t0": 63.05, "t1": 65.59, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Fraud found: fell to 2023, then rose", "kicker": "The second lead"}, "emph": ["fell"], "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.43, 0.71, 1.07, 1.37, 1.77, 2.03]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1]"], "text": "In 2019, investigators found 307,201 dollars.", "t0": 65.71, "t1": 70.06, "shot": "b13", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "magnifier", "label": "Fraud found", "kicker": "The second lead"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.44, 0.9, 1.5, 1.73, 1.98, 2.34, 2.65, 3.07, 3.25, 3.57, 3.78]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what"], "text": "By 2023, the caseload had more than doubled. How much fraud did they find then?", "t0": 70.18, "t1": 75.27, "shot": "b14", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "question", "label": "Fiscal 2023", "kicker": "The second lead"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.45, 0.97, 1.07, 1.52, 1.68, 1.87, 2.03, 2.89, 3.1, 3.32, 3.64, 3.76, 3.9, 4.15]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[1].what", "story[2]"], "text": "165,985 dollars.", "t0": 75.27, "t1": 78.38, "shot": "b15", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "$165,985", "label": "fraud identified, fiscal 2023", "sub": "about half of 2019"}, "emph": ["165,985"], "wt": [0.04, 0.25, 0.56, 1.13, 1.56, 1.78, 2.09, 2.59]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[1].why", "suspicious[1].what"], "text": "By 2026, it was the highest of the three. As a share, it halved.", "t0": 78.9, "t1": 83.12, "shot": "b15r", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Fraud identified, as a share of benefits", "rows": [["fiscal 2019", "$307,201 · 0.39%"], ["fiscal 2023", "$165,985 · 0.08%"], ["fiscal 2026", "$466,321 · 0.19%"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.41, 0.99, 1.09, 1.21, 1.32, 1.71, 1.81, 1.91, 2.78, 3.0, 3.09, 3.55, 3.74]}, {"scene": "lead2", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[1].why"], "text": "Why would it fall? Either fraud became rarer, or less of it was looked for. The records can’t tell which.", "t0": 83.24, "t1": 89.31, "shot": "b16", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "Either fraud became rarer or less of it was looked for"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.21, 0.37, 0.47, 1.45, 1.76, 2.1, 2.45, 2.92, 3.13, 3.36, 3.44, 3.54, 3.67, 3.92, 4.62, 4.8, 5.17, 5.44, 5.68]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "count", "ref": ["suspicious[2]"], "text": "The third lead is penalties. In 2026, investigators found evidence in 598 cases.", "t0": 89.53, "t1": 95.73, "shot": "b17", "visual": {"type": "count", "value": "598", "label": "investigations that found evidence, fiscal 2026"}, "emph": ["598"], "wt": [0.0, 0.14, 0.42, 0.68, 0.82, 2.04, 2.22, 2.49, 3.07, 3.7, 3.96, 4.36, 4.49, 4.79, 5.11, 5.6]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["suspicious[2].why"], "text": "The program’s own penalty is being cut off from food aid. How many people got it?", "t0": 95.85, "t1": 99.73, "shot": "b18", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "A disqualification is the program’s own penalty for intentional violation"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.11, 0.57, 0.74, 1.14, 1.23, 1.43, 1.62, 1.74, 1.93, 2.19, 2.81, 2.98, 3.14, 3.38, 3.6]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "bignum", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "story[3]"], "text": "Between 3 and 30.", "t0": 99.73, "t1": 100.87, "shot": "b19", "visual": {"type": "bignum", "value": "3–30", "label": "people disqualified, fiscal 2026", "sub": "the State hides counts under 11"}, "emph": ["Between"], "wt": [0.04, 0.42, 0.66, 0.77]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "scene", "ref": ["suspicious[2].what", "established[6]"], "text": "And through prosecution? No one, in 7 of the last 8 years.", "t0": 101.39, "t1": 105.24, "shot": "b20", "visual": {"type": "scene", "art": "gavel", "label": "Through prosecution: 0", "kicker": "The third lead", "sub": "food aid only; the DA lists 71 welfare-fraud cases since 2011, all aid programs"}, "emph": ["No one"], "wt": [0.0, 0.13, 0.34, 1.69, 1.94, 2.22, 2.43, 2.75, 2.84, 2.94, 3.2, 3.42]}, {"scene": "lead3", "kind": "quote", "ref": ["notEstablished[2]"], "text": "Why so few? Cases may end in repayment deals. These reports don’t count those.", "t0": 105.36, "t1": 109.91, "shot": "b21", "visual": {"type": "quote", "line": "cases may be settled by repayment agreements that these reports do not count"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.28, 0.5, 1.33, 1.75, 1.95, 2.11, 2.21, 2.66, 3.09, 3.32, 3.67, 3.9, 4.16]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[3]"], "text": "Per 10,000 households, San Francisco closed 171 investigations.", "t0": 110.13, "t1": 114.55, "shot": "b22", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Investigations per 10,000 households, fiscal 2026", "rows": [["San Bernardino", "550"], ["California", "255"], ["San Francisco", "171"]]}, "emph": ["171"], "wt": [0.0, 0.16, 0.36, 0.73, 1.23, 1.45, 1.92, 2.28, 2.47, 2.81, 3.4]}, {"scene": "lead4", "kind": "rank", "ref": ["suspicious[3]"], "text": "San Bernardino closed 550.", "t0": 114.67, "t1": 116.57, "shot": "b22", "visual": {"type": "rank", "label": "Investigations per 10,000 households, fiscal 2026", "rows": [["San Bernardino", "550"], ["California", "255"], ["San Francisco", "171"]]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.23, 0.7, 1.0, 1.24, 1.47]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "unknowns", "ref": ["notEstablished[1]", "notEstablished[0]"], "text": "The records don’t show that fraud is more common here, or less. Or how much of the error was overpaid.", "t0": 116.79, "t1": 122.35, "shot": "b23", "visual": {"type": "unknowns", "cards": ["That fraud is more common here, or less", "How much error was overpayment", "Whether the running 5% will hold to September 2026"]}, "wt": [0.0, 0.12, 0.46, 0.71, 0.96, 1.1, 1.4, 1.51, 1.71, 2.08, 2.52, 2.76, 3.74, 3.95, 4.09, 4.27, 4.35, 4.47, 4.74, 4.89]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[2]", "next[3]"], "text": "What would settle it? The error rate split by cause.", "t0": 122.47, "t1": 126.03, "shot": "b24", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "Error rate split by overpayment and cause"}, {"who": "", "what": "Cases settled by repayment"}, {"who": "", "what": "What the State will owe from 2028"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.0, 0.17, 0.34, 0.65, 1.39, 1.62, 1.91, 2.2, 2.54, 2.71]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "settle", "ref": ["next[0]", "next[2]", "next[3]"], "text": "Cases settled by repayment. And what the State will owe.", "t0": 126.03, "t1": 129.45, "shot": "b24", "visual": {"type": "settle", "cards": [{"who": "", "what": "Error rate split by overpayment and cause"}, {"who": "", "what": "Cases settled by repayment"}, {"who": "", "what": "What the State will owe from 2028"}], "focus": 0}, "wt": [0.04, 0.5, 0.8, 0.98, 1.96, 2.18, 2.4, 2.51, 2.83, 3.1]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "status", "ref": ["status", "established[4]"], "text": "No food-aid audit is on file. A 2016 cash-aid audit found no errors.", "t0": 129.57, "t1": 134.18, "shot": "b25", "visual": {"type": "status"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.26, 0.65, 0.94, 1.09, 1.25, 2.03, 2.17, 2.47, 2.93, 3.4, 3.69, 3.93, 4.11]}, {"scene": "close", "kind": "end", "ref": ["end"], "text": "A lead is a question, not an accusation.", "t0": 134.3, "t1": 136.23, "shot": "b26", "visual": {"type": "end"}, "wt": [0.0, 0.15, 0.38, 0.48, 0.53, 0.96, 1.13, 1.21]}], "format": 6, "chapters": {"open": "The question", "found": "On the record", "lead1": "Lead 1 · the error rate", "lead2": "Lead 2 · fraud found fell", "lead3": "Lead 3 · almost no penalties", "lead4": "Lead 4 · effort", "close": "Where it stands"}, "look": "terminal", "hook": "question"}